<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kadungon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 560–590</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kadungon was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> king of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the late 6th century who, according to the Velvikudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> plates, ended the rule of the Kalabhras and restored Pandya power at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>. He is regarded as the founder of the First Pandyan Empire, which, with the Pallavas to the north, dominated Tamil country for the next three centuries.</p></div>
